  "All runs use --conserve with u<=dep and the same-hour arrival convention: arrivals at t come only from served departures at t, weighted by the row-normalised Q1 (or observed) P.",
  "u=0 scenarios reproduce the T006 R1 smoke rows bit-for-bit: q1 alpha=1 K=60 moved 24,679.2791, truck-km 5,529.8473, dev 225.3579, obj 82,194.7968; obs 23,959.1518 / 5,440.9441 / 900.0000 / 83,325.2404. With u=0, conserve changes no arrival.",
  "Conservation is exact to solver tolerance: the largest city residual is 3.23e-9 (alpha=0.6), the largest zone residual 3.97e-10, and the day-end city difference 7.39e-9; all below 1e-6.",
  "Unmet appears only when the initial fleet is scaled: alpha=0.8 K=80 has 447.52 unmet, alpha=0.6 K=80 has 59,517.66. The LP trades unmet against end-of-day deviation; dev is not equal to unmet in either row.",
  "Scenario coverage is alpha=1 K=20/40/60/80 plus alpha=0.8/0.6 at K=80. The full alpha=0.4-1.0 x K grid was NOT run and is marked in q2_results_q1.json; T012 must not quote unrun grid values.",
  "K=20 and K=40 are capacity-binding: moved is exactly 9,600 and 19,200 bikes; K=60 moves 24,679 and K=80 only 24,753, so the returns flatten above K=60.",
  "H14: greedy max hourly moved is 623.17 (limit 2,400) and max source ratio exactly 40 bikes/truck (limit 40), with zero violations. Trucks start each hour summing to K and move with their bikes.",
  "Night (21:00-06:00, 9 h) carries 39.34% of moved bikes and 37.12% of truck-km, close to its 37.5% share of clock time; the paper's 'daytime barely moves' wording is not supported. No night cost was added.",
  "The stochastic simulation reports 0.00% unmet for every policy and alpha, including no trucks: with I0 ~343,638 the zone inventories never hit zero at 5-min resolution, so the simulation is uninformative about the LP's alpha<1 unmet. This is a known limitation, not evidence that unmet is zero.",
